    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d367">

                <pb facs="0433" n="1167" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1167"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. Dupuy de Lôme.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-06-24"><hi rendition="#italic">June 24,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 11.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In answer to a telegraphic dispatch from
                    this Department, the United States minister at Madrid wires that the sensational
                    articles in the Times and other New York papers, to which you referred at our
                    interview of the other day, are perfectly understood in Madrid to be merely
                    rumors, for which this Government is in no way responsible.</p>
                <p>Awaiting information respecting the answer to your telegram to Madrid, of which
                    you were good enough to apprise me, I take this opportunity, etc.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
